[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Snake Poison]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.77]Lesson 20 | 第20课
[00:02.24]Snake poison | 蛇毒
[00:08.79]What are the two different ways in which snake poison acts? | 蛇毒起作用有哪两种不同的方式？
[00:15.32]How in came about that snakes manufactured poison is a mystery. | 蛇是怎样产生蛇毒的，这是一个谜。
[00:20.33]Over the periods their saliva, a mild, digestive juice like our own, was converted into a poison that defies analysis even today. | 经过漫长的岁月，蛇的唾液——一种和我们的唾液一样的温和的消化液——变成了一种连今天也难以分析的毒液。
[00:30.46]It was not forced upon them by the survival competition; | 这并不是生存竞争强加给它们的；
[00:34.46]they could have caught and lived on prey without using poison, just as the thousands of non-poisonous snakes still do. | 它们本可以不用毒液捕捉并赖以为生地吃掉猎物，就像数千种无毒蛇现在仍然做的那样。
[00:42.76]Poison to a snake is merely a luxury; | 毒液对蛇来说只是一种奢侈的享受；
[00:46.30]it enables it to get its food with very little effort, no more effort than one bite. | 它使蛇不费什么力气就能得到食物，顶多咬一口而已。
[00:53.08]And why only snakes? | 那为什么只有蛇有呢？
[00:55.48]Cats, for instance, would be greatly helped; | 比如说，猫如果有了毒液将受益极大：
[00:58.32]no running fights with large, fierce rats or tussles with grown rabbits--just a bite and no more effort needed. | 不必再和大而凶猛的老鼠进行追逐搏斗，也不必再和成年的兔子扭打——只咬一口，再不必费力气。
[01:06.56]In fact, it would be an assistance to all carnivores though it would be a two-edged weapon when they fought each other. | 事实上，毒液对一切食肉动物都有帮助，虽然当食肉动物相互残杀时，它会成为一柄双刃剑。
[01:14.26]But, of the vertebrates unpredictable Nature selected only snakes (and one lizard). | 但是，在脊椎动物当中，反复无常的大自然只选择了蛇（和一种蜥蜴）。
[01:20.85]One wonders also why Nature, with some snakes concocted poison of such extreme potency. | 人们还感到奇怪的是，大自然为何让某些蛇调配出效力极强的毒液。
[01:28.19]In the conversion of saliva into poison, one might suppose that a fixed process took place. It did not; | 在唾液转变成毒液的过程中，人们可能以为有一个固定的过程。其实没有；
[01:36.06]some snakes manufactured a poison different in every respect from that of others, | 有些蛇制造的毒液与其他蛇的毒液在各方面都截然不同，
[01:41.47]as different as arsenic is from strychnine, and having different effects. | 就像砒霜之于马钱子碱，各有不同的效果。
[01:47.07]One poison acts on the nerves, the other on the blood. | 一种毒液作用于神经，另一种作用于血液。
[01:51.50]The makers of the nerve poison include the mambas and the cobras and their venom is called neurotoxic. | 制造神经毒液的蛇包括曼巴蛇和眼镜蛇，它们的毒液叫作神经毒素。
[01:59.29]Vipers (adders) and rattlesnakes manufacture the blood poison, which is known as haemolytic. | 蝰蛇（小蝰蛇）和响尾蛇制造血液毒液，即所谓的溶血毒液。
[02:07.07]Both poisons are unpleasant, but by far the more unpleasant is the blood poison. | 两种毒液都不好受，但相比之下血液毒液更糟。
[02:12.61]It is said that the nerve poison is the more primitive of the two, that the blood poison is, so to speak, a newer product from an improved formula. | 据说神经毒液是两者中较为原始的一种，而血液毒液，可以这么说，是改良配方的新产品。
[02:22.08]Be that as it may, the nerve poison does its business with man far more quickly than the blood poison. | 尽管如此，神经毒液对付人比血液毒液快得多。
[02:28.44]This, however, means nothing. | 然而，这说明不了什么。
[02:30.85]Snakes did not acquire their poison for use against man but for use against prey such as rats and mice, | 蛇获得毒液不是为了用来对付人，而是为了对付老鼠这样的猎物，
[02:38.20]and the effects on these of viperine poison is almost immediate. | 而蝰蛇的毒液对这些猎物的作用几乎是立竿见影的。
